  "title": "DK Metcalf Reenacts Michael Jordan's 1984 Cradle Dunk At UNC Against Terrapins",
  "htmlContent": "<!-- wp:image {\"id\":510612,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/02/GettyImages-1282363946-1-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-510612\"/><figcaption> (Photo by Christian Petersen/Getty Images)</figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Seattle Seahawks wide receiver DK Metcalf had arguably the best defensive play of the season. He chased down Budda Baker. After a Russell Wilson interception on Oct 25, 2020, against the Arizona Cardinals, and saving a pick-six. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9ImdWvuzsCY\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9ImdWvuzsCY\n</div><figcaption><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>He also made a couple of other spectator plays for the Seahaw<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span>ks this past season. Such as hurdling Eagles defender Darius Slay; he also caught a one-handed pass in pre-game before the Seahawks home game. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Et27d6hgZjw\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Et27d6hgZjw\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>This off-season, DK Metcalf is continuing to make jaw-dropping plays, but this time it is on the basketball court as he reenacts Michael Jordan's 1984 cradle dunk on the Maryland Terrapins. <g<span style=\"font-size:0px; color:#ff0000;\">﻿\n</span>wmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://twitter.com/overtime/status/1363258215379664896?s=20\",\"type\":\"rich\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"twitter\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-twitter wp-block-embed-twitter\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://twitter.com/overtime/status/1363258215379664896?s=20\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Seahawks started the season with six and 0 records and won the NFC West Division this past season but fell short in the first round of the playoffs. The Seahawks have some tough decisions to make this off-season, such as resigning Chris Carson, Jarran Reed, KJ Wright, and others. Seattle also has to deal with a disgruntled Russell Wilson, who spoke out  about all the hits he took over the years from not having an offensive line last month. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->",
